# Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  L[Governed landing files] --> B[Bronze raw]
  B --> S[Silver curated]
  S --> G[Gold model inputs]
  G --> T[Training and evaluation]
  T --> M[Unity Catalog model version]
  M --> I[Batch inference]
  G --> I
  I --> P[Prediction history]
  P --> O[Monitoring metrics and reports]
```

{% if workspace_topology == 'separate_workspaces' %}
The selected topology uses separate DEV, QA and PROD workspaces and catalogs.
{% else %}
The selected topology uses one workspace with separate DEV, QA and PROD catalogs.
Catalog separation in one workspace provides less isolation than separate workspaces.
Configure catalog grants deliberately; bundle targets are not a security boundary.
{% endif %}
Use workspace-catalog bindings and intentional grants to restrict PROD access.
A shared metastore permits approved cross-catalog model copies; different metastores
need an artifact export/import process with provenance and checksum verification.

Every catalog has project-prefixed schemas: `landing`, `bronze`, `silver`, `gold`,
`models`, `predictions`, `monitoring`. The landing schema holds a governed volume,
not a table of files. Prediction outputs are separate from Gold feature inputs.
Bundle targets select deployment settings; grants and bindings enforce isolation.
